  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Combined-arms manoeuvre built on air superiority, precision fires, ISR drones and night-vision overmatch. Army brigades are armored (Abrams/Bradley), Stryker or infantry (light/airborne/air assault); the Marine Corps is reorganising under Force Design into lighter, ship-based littoral units (tanks divested 2021, AAV retired 2025, ACV and JLTV in their place). In counter-terror work: small raid forces, helicopter assault, overwhelming fire support and casualty evacuation inside the 'golden hour'.",
    "squad_size": 9,
    "fireteam": "US Army rifle squad: squad leader + two 4-man fireteams (team leader, automatic rifleman, grenadier, rifleman). USMC squad under Force Design: squad leader, assistant squad leader, squad systems operator (drones/EW) + three 3-man fireteams (team leader, automatic rifleman with M27, rifleman). In game: 8-man squads in 4 battle-buddy pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Bounding overwatch by pairs and fireteams; base-of-fire plus manoeuvre element",
      "Night raids with full NVG and IR laser/illuminator use; prefer to fight at night",
      "Calls for fire early: mortars, artillery, attack helicopters, armed drones",
      "Room clearing with flashbangs and frags, stacking in pairs",
      "Smoke to screen casualty extraction; aggressive CASEVAC by UH-60 MEDEVAC",
      "Mounted patrols in MRAPs/JLTVs with route clearance; dismount on contact",
      "Drone ISR overwatch of the objective before and during the assault"
    ],
